1621,"name":"Donna Weaver","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/4673920-donna-weaver","contributor":{"__ref":"Contributor:kca://author/amzn1.gr.author.v1.dZqzy0Q6fCoEXDh1I1tuRQ"},"id":4673920},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2PLJMTWBIUGI3":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2PLJMTWBIUGI3"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2PLJMTWBIUGI3\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.ZrOFHbel79IK_xWyn3gS3Q\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2PLJMTWBIUGI3","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2PLJMTWBIUGI3"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.ZrOFHbel79IK_xWyn3gS3Q","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.ZrOFHbel79IK_xWyn3gS3Q"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/4673920?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/6377315152"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v2.2024032700.24ed53fb-50d6-46ba-9b30-e390a45b7257":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v2.2024032700.24ed53fb-50d6-46ba-9b30-e390a45b7257","creator":{"__ref":"User:4673920"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1711499516423,"createdAt":1711497872908,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1711499516266,"text":"WHAT IT'S ABOUT\u003cbr /\u003ein the Royal States of America, magic rules all, but life—and love—always finds a way.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eLatent horse empath. Dishwasher. Closet chef. Future king. When food poisoning sweeps through Dallas, Patrick Laycal doesn't expect a princess to show up at his door asking for his help. Her one, simple request dumps him in the middle of a Royal mess—one that could cost him far more than just his life.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eMY TAKE\u003cbr /\u003eThis was an interesting take on a dystopian America. Pat's such a mellow, solid character man. He's such a hard worker and smart. Unfortunately, the world has levels of magic and he's in the lowest cast. Which means he and his family have the fewest opportunities. The society even expressly limits how far someone in a cast system can rise.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eHe works as a dishwasher, though he's attending culinary school. When royals decide to slum it and eat food like \"regular\" people, he has an opportunity to cook. And ends up doing a better job than his boss. When he changes Pat's schedule, giving him 3 days off without pay (punishing instead of rewarding him), Pat decides to quit rather than be fired.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnd that's when things really change for him. He gets a job offer as a custodian this time with a crazy company I didn't fully understand but was full of slobby but kind people. And they love his cooking too. They have something to do with horses, and Pat discovers he's more than a mild horse empath. But things get really crazy when the royal princess tracks him down from that day when he cooked for them. She jokingly asks him to marry her and that he needs to cook for her.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eIt's a crazy series of events, but it's a sweet love story, though Pat ends up spending more time thinking about the heir to the throne than actually spending time with her. It also feels like he spends more time with horses in the book than with her. But it manages to work, and I found the time entertaining with both. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThere's talk about sex but no on screen time. The princess has a real potty mouth. Pat does too but to a lesser degree.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e4 1/2 stars\u003cbr /\u003e","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2PLJMTWBIUGI3\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.ZrOFHbel79IK_xWyn3gS3Q\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:1628347":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":1628347,"imageUrlSquare":"","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":8,"textReviewsCount":823,"name":"Kari Chapman","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/1628347-kari-chapman","contributor":null,"id":1628347},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A31YFYTUUMEVK3":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A31YFYTUUMEVK3"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A31YFYTUUMEVK3\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.ZrOFHbel79IK_xWyn3gS3Q\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A31YFYTUUMEVK3","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A31YFYTUUMEVK3"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.ZrOFHbel79IK_xWyn3gS3Q","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.ZrOFHbel79IK_xWyn3gS3Q"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"did-not-finish","displayName":"Did Not Finish","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_dnf","sortOrder":3,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/1628347?shelf=did-not-finish"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/7437879382"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.Gv90L82nGqe0eJxqyGD5UA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.Gv90L82nGqe0eJxqyGD5UA","creator":{"__ref":"User:1628347"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1743957647640,"createdAt":1743956944935,"spoilerStatus":true,"lastRevisionAt":1743957647482,"text":"This started strong enough for me to buy the book at the end of the free sample. I liked the main characters, and I appreciated the change up to a wealthy woman and the male lead is the poor but brilliant person who just needs a shot to make it big. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eHowever, after a while the ridiculousness of this world just got to be too much for me. Basically the author is trying to set our male lead up as an unrecognized genius, but everything that he's finding should have been found well before he comes on the scene. All those rich people, including the Queen are getting routinely sick and no one is investigating? He gets it figured out in less than 24 hours, and it's just \"Some stupid food company didn't check to see if all parts of the asparagus plant are edible\". And during his \"interview\" for his new job, he points out that someone that keeps wrecking kitchen equipment might have an electricity power. Given apparently anyone can get tested whenever, and powers can get you upward mobility, how would this already well off man not be aware of that already? \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnd then there's the new job. What part of any of that makes sense in any world? A janitor gets interviewed with big wigs, is given an education fund, a horse, and will be cooking for them as well? Why even? I know, they try to justify it with basically these are good people, but how does any of that make business sense? ","rating":1,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A31YFYTUUMEVK3\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.ZrOFHbel79IK_xWyn3gS3Q\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:26958286":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":26958286,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1464713851i/26958286._UY200_CR46,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":0,"textReviewsCount":335,"name":"Kelly","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/26958286-kelly","contributor":null,"id":26958286},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1LB6EO4EUEHJT":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1LB6EO4EUEHJT"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1LB6EO4EUEHJT\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.ZrOFHbel79IK_xWyn3gS3Q\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1LB6EO4EUEHJT","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1LB6EO4EUEHJT"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.ZrOFHbel79IK_xWyn3gS3Q","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.ZrOFHbel79IK_xWyn3gS3Q"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/26958286?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2858943103"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.YxXoIY68ohSPylbFFphQvw":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.YxXoIY68ohSPylbFFphQvw","creator":{"__ref":"User:26958286"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1560606894938,"createdAt":1560606138987,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1560606894591,"text":"\u003cstrong\u003eDecent background; little plot. \u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI hope, after this, Copperfield will quit classifying these books as dystopic--they are the opposite of dystopic, where the everyman can have education and upward social movement, and most importantly, choice over how to live their lives. \u003cbr /\u003eThe repeated use of ain't bothered me. It certainly doesn't make the characters sound \"country,\" nor does it mimic any sort of accent. It just makes them-- Pat included, based on his other vocabulary--sound like pretentious people trying to live down with the unwashed masses. \u003cbr /\u003eWhile not a flaw, this is entirely a character-driven book, light on plot. It is simply to get to know a couple of other voices from \"Null and Void\" without giving them a true story of their own. There are significant breaks from the storyline established in that first novel--while they don't diminish from the story, they are noticeable. ","rating":3,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1LB6EO4EUEHJT\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.ZrOFHbel79IK_xWyn3gS3Q\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"v